{"path":"doc/tutorial/workspaces","title":"Tutorial: Getting started with multi-module workspaces","description":"This tutorial introduces the basics of multi-module workspaces in Go. With multi-module workspaces, you can tell the Go command that you’re writing code in multiple modules at the same time and easily…","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tutorial: Getting started with multi-module workspaces"}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"nav"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This tutorial introduces the basics of multi-module workspaces in Go. With multi-module workspaces, you can tell the Go command that you’re writing code in multiple modules at the same time and easily build and run code in those modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this tutorial, you’ll create two modules in a shared multi-module workspace, make changes across those modules, and see the results of those changes in a build."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" For other tutorials, see "},{"type":"link","href":"https://go.dev/doc/tutorial/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tutorials"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"prerequisites","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerequisites"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Go."}]},{"type":"text","value":" We recommend using the latest version of Go to follow this tutorial. For installation instructions, see "},{"type":"link","href":"doc/install","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installing Go"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A tool to edit your code."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Any text editor you have will work fine."}]},{"children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A command terminal."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Go works well using any terminal on Linux and Mac, and on PowerShell or cmd in Windows."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"create_folder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a module for your code"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To begin, create a module for the code you’ll write."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open a command prompt and change to your home directory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Linux or Mac:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ cd"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Windows:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"C:\\> cd %HOMEPATH%"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rest of the tutorial will show a $ as the prompt. The commands you use will work on Windows too."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From the command prompt, create a directory for your code called workspace."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ mkdir workspace\n$ cd workspace"}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initialize the module"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Our example will create a new module "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"hello"},{"type":"text","value":" that will depend on the golang.org/x/example module."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the hello module:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ mkdir hello\n$ cd hello\n$ go mod init example.com/hello\ngo: creating new go.mod: module example.com/hello"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add a dependency on the golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse package by using "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go get"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ go get golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create hello.go in the hello directory with the following contents:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"package main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n\n    \"golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(reverse.String(\"Hello\"))\n}"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now, run the hello program:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ go run .\nolleH"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"create-the-workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the workspace"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this step, we’ll create a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file to specify a workspace with the module."}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":"initialize-the-workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initialize the workspace"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" directory, run:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ go work init ./hello"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go work init"},{"type":"text","value":" command tells "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" to create a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file for a workspace containing the modules in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"./hello"},{"type":"text","value":" directory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" command produces a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file that looks like this:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"go 1.18\n\nuse ./hello"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file has similar syntax to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.mod"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" directive tells Go which version of Go the file should be interpreted with. It’s similar to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" directive in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.mod"},{"type":"text","value":" file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"use"},{"type":"text","value":" directive tells Go that the module in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"hello"},{"type":"text","value":" directory should be main modules when doing a build."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So in any subdirectory of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" the module will be active."}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":"run-the-program-in-the-workspace-directory","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the program in the workspace directory"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace"},{"type":"text","value":" directory, run:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ go run ./hello\nolleH"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Go command includes all the modules in the workspace as main modules. This allows us to refer to a package in the module, even outside the module. Running the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go run"},{"type":"text","value":" command outside the module or the workspace would result in an error because the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" command wouldn’t know which modules to use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next, we’ll add a local copy of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module to the workspace. That module is stored in a subdirectory of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.googlesource.com/example"},{"type":"text","value":" Git repository. We’ll then add a new function to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"reverse"},{"type":"text","value":" package that we can use instead of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"String"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"download-and-modify-the-golangorgxexamplehello-module","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download and modify the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this step, we’ll download a copy of the Git repo containing the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module, add it to the workspace, and then add a new function to it that we will use from the hello program."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clone the repository"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From the workspace directory, run the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"git"},{"type":"text","value":" command to clone the repository:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ git clone https://go.googlesource.com/example\nCloning into 'example'...\nremote: Total 165 (delta 27), reused 165 (delta 27)\nReceiving objects: 100% (165/165), 434.18 KiB | 1022.00 KiB/s, done.\nResolving deltas: 100% (27/27), done."}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the module to the workspace"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Git repo was just checked out into "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"./example"},{"type":"text","value":". The source code for the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module is in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"./example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":". Add it to the workspace:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ go work use ./example/hello"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go work use"},{"type":"text","value":" command adds a new module to the go.work file. It will now look like this:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"go 1.18\n\nuse (\n    ./hello\n    ./example/hello\n)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The workspace now includes both the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"example.com/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module and the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module, which provides the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse"},{"type":"text","value":" package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This will allow us to use the new code we will write in our copy of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"reverse"},{"type":"text","value":" package instead of the version of the package in the module cache that we downloaded with the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go get"},{"type":"text","value":" command."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add the new function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll add a new function to reverse a number to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse"},{"type":"text","value":" package."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a new file named "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"int.go"},{"type":"text","value":" in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace/example/hello/reverse"},{"type":"text","value":" directory containing the following contents:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"package reverse\n\nimport \"strconv\"\n\n// Int returns the decimal reversal of the integer i.\nfunc Int(i int) int {\n    i, _ = strconv.Atoi(String(strconv.Itoa(i)))\n    return i\n}"}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modify the hello program to use the function."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modify the contents of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"workspace/hello/hello.go"},{"type":"text","value":" to contain the following contents:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"package main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n\n    \"golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(reverse.String(\"Hello\"), reverse.Int(24601))\n}"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":"run-the-code-in-the-workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the code in the workspace"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From the workspace directory, run"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"$ go run ./hello\nolleH 10642"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Go command finds the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"example.com/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module specified in the command line in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"hello"},{"type":"text","value":" directory specified by the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file, and similarly resolves the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello/reverse"},{"type":"text","value":" import using the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" can be used instead of adding "},{"type":"link","href":"https://go.dev/ref/mod#go-mod-file-replace","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"replace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" directives to work across multiple modules."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since the two modules are in the same workspace it’s easy to make a change in one module and use it in another."}]},{"type":"heading","level":4,"id":"future-step","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Future step"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now, to properly release these modules we’d need to make a release of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module, for example at "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"v0.1.0"},{"type":"text","value":". This is usually done by tagging a commit on the module’s version control repository. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://go.dev/doc/modules/release-workflow","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"module release workflow documentation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more details. Once the release is done, we can increase the requirement on the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"golang.org/x/example/hello"},{"type":"text","value":" module in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"hello/go.mod"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"cd hello\ngo get golang.org/x/example/hello@v0.1.0"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That way, the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" command can properly resolve the modules outside the workspace."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"learn-more-about-workspaces","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn more about workspaces"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go"},{"type":"text","value":" command has a couple of subcommands for working with workspaces in addition to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go work init"},{"type":"text","value":" which we saw earlier in the tutorial:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"go work use [-r] [dir]"},{"type":"text","value":" adds a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"use"},{"type":"text","value":" directive to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file for "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"dir"},{"type":"text","value":", if it exists, and removes the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"use"},{"type":"text","value":" directory if the argument directory doesn’t exist. The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"-r"},{"type":"text","value":" flag examines subdirectories of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"dir"},{"type":"text","value":" recursively."}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"go work edit"},{"type":"text","value":" edits the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" file similarly to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go mod edit"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"go work sync"},{"type":"text","value":" syncs dependencies from the workspace’s build list into each of the workspace modules."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"https://go.dev/ref/mod#workspaces","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspaces"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in the Go Modules Reference for more detail on workspaces and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"go.work"},{"type":"text","value":" files."}]}]}}
